>> title: Roast Turkey Breast with Pan Gravy
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hours
>> tags: centerpiece, watchme, poultry, carving, holiday

Pat @bone-in turkey breast{5%lb} dry with #paper towels{}.

Mix @softened butter{4%tbsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @thyme leaves{1%tbsp}, and @lemon zest{1%tsp} in a #bowl{}.

-- watch: Butter is spread evenly under and over the skin without tearing it.
Loosen the turkey skin with your fingers and rub herb butter under the skin and over the outside.

Place @onion{1}, @carrot{1}, and @celery rib{1} in a #roasting pan{} and set turkey on top.

Roast in a 350°F oven for ~{90%minutes}, using a #thermometer{} to verify doneness before resting.

Rest turkey on a #cutting board{} for ~{20%minutes}.

Pour pan drippings into a #measuring cup{} and skim excess fat.

Whisk @flour{2%tbsp} into @butter{2%tbsp} in a #saucepan{} for ~{2%minutes}, then whisk in drippings and @chicken stock{1.5%cups}.

-- watch: Gravy coats the back of a spoon and pours in a smooth ribbon.
Simmer gravy until thickened, about ~{5%minutes}.

-- watch: Knife slices across the grain into even pieces about 1/4 inch thick.
Carve turkey breast from the bone and slice across the grain with a #carving knife{}.
